{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/184864-summer-dominated-freehold","id":184864,"title":"Summer-dominated Freehold","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-30T09:03:11-07:00","id":184864,"title":"Summer-dominated Freehold","content":"I decided to do something different for my next game and have a summer-dominated freehold. Not Endless Summer, just a strong court that's front and center on the political scene because - well, I'm not sure about the reason for now. I'm an Autumn fan, and Summer always struck me as too straightforward; I can't come up with interesting stuff to do with them, especially given that it's been relatively quiet in the Hedge lately, so their military side is not that prominent.<br /> <br /> So I humbly request assistance. Assuming the Summer Monarch is strong and intelligent with their resources, what would the Summer Court's function in a freehold be, aside from fighting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3316-cantshutup","name":"cantshutup","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T12:18:40-07:00","id":184984,"title":"","content":"Ha, I've managed to pull off a Summer coup in my game! I would say that a Summer freehold would be stricter than most - forced to formally join a Court and register with a motley, Summer motleys often patrol or leep the peace, a strict curfew - things like that. A freehold ruled by a Summer monarch would be like a bastion, a fortress; the Fae will /never/ be allowed to breach it and hurt them again, and everything goes to that purpose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T14:25:11-07:00","id":185053,"title":"","content":"There are a lot of ways one that can approach the Summer Court's mission. Given that allegiance to a Seasonal Court does not necessarily mean that one is somehow part of a vast conspiracy of interconnected freeholds, there is a ton of freedom when it comes to how a given Court approaches the Seasonal dogma.<br /> <br /> Like Atamajakki said, you can go with the super fascist interpretation of Summer, with a host of prohibitions and a regimented, military like social hierarchy. <br /> <br /> You can go the opposite route and have the Summer courtiers work like an activist/anarchy association. Fiercely individualistic, they would channel the anger of those who were subjugated by the Gentry into a general hatred of all Institutions of Control. They gather in cells, and their Crown never stays with the same changeling from season to season, and fight against the corruption of the other Courts and social injustice in the world around them. <br /> <br /> In one short game, the Summer Court in the freehold was modeled after Evangelical Christian Churches. They gathered at a Church Hollow deep in the Hedge every Sunday to listen to the fiery sermons of the Reverend, a charismatic changeling who wears the Crown of Summer and whose tears were said to cure madness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T14:44:49-07:00","id":185063,"title":"","content":"My current chronicle has the militarized approach I discussed earlier, but the next game has them as little more than a disorganized guerilla force. There's no hierarchy; individual motleys work as what seem mostly like Hunter cells, hiding in cover until they can strike out against hobgoblins, loyalists, privateers, and anyone they decide they don't like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T15:15:01-07:00","id":185151,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... I'm currently thinking about a very pragmatic Summer queen that runs everything according to plan, covering all the bases. There's a hedge fortress with people always on watch, there are several human-world businesses that employ a lot of freehold's changelings, there are ensorcelled and pledge-bound mortals in positions of power in the city... The court itself will take anyone in, because anyone can be an asset, and anyone has things to contribute. Other courts are assessed on their usefulness too - Spring has connections, and Winter has information, and Autumn has magic - but if any court fails to contribute to the 'common good' Summer starts polishing their sticks meaningfully and talking about &quot;working together in the face of the Fae threat&quot;. <br /> <br /> I suppose it's closer to the 'militarized' concept, but I see the court as more of a court of business in peacetime, very human-facing. There's a construction company and an exclusive restaurant run jointly with Spring horticulturalists, and a city-famous sports bar ran by an old giant ogre that likes dirty drinking songs...<br /> <br /> And when trouble comes to town, all those landscaping designers and waiters and the middleschool gym teacher take up their weapons and kick its ass <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3316-cantshutup","name":"cantshutup","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}